<!--Post: 904--><!--Time: 1093521782-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST904"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 5:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom: Good job on the enhancement of the photo. I think that the symbol and the wording were probably embroidered and that is why they appear crude. The hairstyle is typical of the &#39;40&#39;s and early &#39;50&#39;s styles for babies. I have an identical style in some early pics of myself. The folds on the eyes and the base of the nose look like Ms. Vian&#39;s. It appears that there was something written in the corner that was cut off. <BR> <BR>Surely, the police would have contacted victims&#39; families when they received the pic and asked for information to match or id it.  <BR> <BR>Even though it says junior, people exchanged and passed down baby clothes to save money. If this was a sleeper, it would not matter whether the label matched the sex or not. <BR> <BR>BTK is enough of an egomaniac to send a pic of himself. If that is him, you can bet that he has no close family living in the area who could id it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 904-->
<!--Post: 909--><!--Time: 1093541743-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST909"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Colette<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Colette<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 10:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The symbol looks like a pair of boxing gloves.I remember reading that Mr. Otero was a boxer, possibly has father was also..therefore &#34;junior/boxing gloves&#34; on the baby shirt.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 909-->
<!--Post: 910--><!--Time: 1093552172-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST910"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rachel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rachel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 26, 2004 - 1:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great shot of the picture, Tom! <BR> <BR>For some reason, the symbol looks like a sideways snail to me...?? Be gentle. <BR> <BR>Rachel<!--/Text--></td></tr>
