<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bargle<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bargle<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, November 22, 2004 - 4:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s my take on the photo. <BR>To me the animal looks like a dog or beaver wearing a party hat. I notice there is something else to the right of the animal head. Maybe a part of the tail?  <BR>The writing looks like Juansa or maybe Juanisa. I did a Google search on both names and they seem to be legitimate female Spanish names. <BR>If &#40;big if&#41; I&#39;m right about the word being Juansa or Juanisa, then maybe this picture came from the Otero&#39;s. Possibly one of their Puerto Rican relative&#39;s child. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
