<!--Post: 1601--><!--Time: 1102253546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1601"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Copykat<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Copykat<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 05, 2004 - 5:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is my first post and it may have already been discussed, but has Charlie Otero ever been shown the picture?  If it is an Otero child, he may be able to identify it. I agree with Bargle--when I first studied the photo, I saw the name &#34;Juansa&#34; or something similar.  However, after reading the posts from people who saw the word &#34;Junior&#34;, I could see that also. <BR> <BR> I also agree that the writing/image were embroidered by hand, as they appear to be rather amateurish.  It was mentioned here that Mr. Otero and his father had both been boxers, and with that information I can see boxing gloves on the sleeper.  But I&#39;m not convinced of it. <BR> <BR>If it hasn&#39;t been done &#40;and according to the interview with him it has not&#41; LE should interview Charlie Otero and pick his brain...did his mother/grandmother/aunt etc. do embroidery work?  Does he recognize the baby in the photo?  Was boxing a subject of particular pride in the family...hence boxing gloves on the sleeper?  Charlie might even recognize the sleeper and what&#39;s written on it~! I think Charlie could be a valuable source of clues, and if I was LE, I&#39;d be questioning him thoroughly--perhaps even using hypnosis to call up subconscious memories. <BR> <BR>Maybe this has already been done &amp; discussed and I&#39;m being redundant in my ignorance.  If so, I apologize~!  Thanks~! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1601-->
<!--Post: 1615--><!--Time: 1102339383-->
