<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3681"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have invested way too much time in photoshop with this picture - but I now think it is a pair of ballet &#34;toe&#34; slippers hanging by their laces. I cut out the part where the crease is in the romper folds and reversed the other side and put them together. Tint the silk parts pink - and it works perfectly. I think it is Julie O - and that her name is embroidered next to the slippers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
