<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3725"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well . . . why is this baby dressed in a winter-like, long-sleeved shirt AND YET have only a diaper thingy on his lower half? <BR> <BR>Why not also put a pair of winter pants on the baby, or conversely put on a short-sleeved shirt? <BR> <BR>The baby doesn&#39;t seemed &#34;dressed properly&#34;; but to that end he/she DOES have exceptionally chubby legs, and maybe they wanted to show that in the pix.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3725-->
<!--Post: 3878--><!--Time: 1105377767-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3878"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Antibtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Antibtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 9:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe that the baby is Joseph Otero,,,looks at the slant in the eyes and the ears are the same and the nose is simular.IMO<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3878-->
<!--Post: 3985--><!--Time: 1105500999-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3985"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 11, 2005 - 7:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Antibtk <BR> <BR>That is an interesting observation.  I never considered the pix could be Joseph Otero because I thought perhaps BTK only savored FEMALE-owned crime souvenirs. <BR> <BR>However, I guess BTK could have taken this photo from the crime scene, or perhaps from one of the Otero’s wallets?   <BR> <BR>DO WE EVEN KNOW IF THIS PHOTO WAS SUBMITTED AS A WALLET-SIZE PHOTO? <BR> <BR>Also, according to reports, Joe Otero was a boxer and the child may have a boxing gloves icon on his shirt. <BR> <BR>The only drawback:  wouldn’t the surviving Otero son &#40;or any relatives&#41; be able to identify this photo? <BR> <BR>Should we safely assume that an age-progression has been done by authorities, and THEY KNOW who it is? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3985-->
<!--Post: 4023--><!--Time: 1105542588-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4023"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Antibtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Antibtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 7:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->but then again he took Joseph Oteros watch as well. <BR> <BR>It is quiet possible that they have done an age-progression on the photo,,Im not quiet sure how effective or accurate that process is beings how I know nothing about it,,, <BR> <BR>some children don&#39;t know what there parents looked like as babies,,can you identify you parents baby pictures??<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4023-->
<!--Post: 4025--><!--Time: 1105544603-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4025"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 7:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Antibk <BR> <BR>You are right.  I probably couldn’t easily identify my parent’s baby pictures if I was shown them “cold” &#40;for the first time&#41;. <BR> <BR>However, if in my lifetime my parents showed me the picture&#40;s&#41; and said “here is my baby picture”; then I probably would remember, or at least get an idea of what they looked like as a baby.   <BR> <BR>I forgot about BTK taking the watch  —  that is a good point.   But I still ask the question:  “Is this a wallet-size photo”?   <BR> <BR>I can see BTK taking a small photo out of a wallet, but I can’t see him running off with a full-size portrait that was perhaps hanging on the wall at the Otero’s home.   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4025-->
<!--Post: 4028--><!--Time: 1105548406-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4028"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iceteajan <BR> <BR>BTK was known to bringing a bag with him. Bowling bag/doctors bag like. <BR>So I guess he could have taken a lager picture than wallet-size. <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4028-->
<!--Post: 4035--><!--Time: 1105555727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4035"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Antibtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Antibtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 10:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m going to guess that if it was a wallet-size photo that it was in a photo album,,usually in my experiences,,photos in my wallet book tend to get lots of wear-n-tear. <BR> <BR>If it is wallet-size and it was taken from a wallet,,then I would more likely believe the picture to be a picture of one of Joseph Oteros kids, because it doesn&#39;t have much wear-n-tear to have lasted in a wallet for several years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4035-->
<!--Post: 4045--><!--Time: 1105566513-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4045"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 12, 2005 - 1:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, there seems no wear-n-tear on the picture, but there are some small rust-like discoloration spots along the right edge and on both legs.   <BR> <BR>But now I’ve noticed one other thing: the side edges appear as if they were trimmed &#40;and not straight!&#41; <BR> <BR>So perhaps this was trimmed from a larger photo? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4045-->
<!--Post: 4497--><!--Time: 1106434675-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4497"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Absinthe1023<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Absinthe1023<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 2:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->First off, great site Tom.  About the pic: <BR>The photo is correctly oriented whent the logo appears on the left breast. <BR>The image is a dog&#39;s head seen from the front, with a drooping right ear that curls around the side of the face.  The dog&#39;s tongue is also protruding. The dog is wearing a pointed cap, with a ball or pompom on the tip.  To the left of the cap &#40;as viewed in the photo&#41;, the script word &#34;Junior&#34; is present.  The word to the right of the cap is obscured by folds, but seems to begin with a tall vertical line.  Does anyone remember a logo of this type for a toy or cartoon/comic figure from that era??  Hope this helps, but I don&#39;t know if the logo itself is at all significant.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4497-->
<!--Post: 4514--><!--Time: 1106455926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 8:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Finally, someone who also says its a dog.  My niece had a baby outfit like that when she was little...it too was a dog...looked exactly like the one in the pic. <BR>thank you absinthe1023<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4514-->
