<!--Post: 6502--><!--Time: 1107834695-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6502"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 7:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I see a rather eerie likeness looking at this tile  compared to the image on the child&#39;s shirt. Remember the child&#39;s shirt is rumpled and arm comes down across part of it. Yes, I can see it being an animal, but just browsing and reading about the beats I ran across this. If this tile were rumpled, can you see it resembling a pair of boxing gloves hanging from a twisted string or rope?  If you enlarge the picture of the tile, don&#39;t git skeered...ok?  <BR><a href="http://prodtn.cafepress.com/3/13288923_F_tn.jpg" target=_top>http://prodtn.cafepress.com/3/13288923_F_tn.jpg</a> <BR> <BR>Does anyone else see the comparison?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
