<!--Post: 7879--><!--Time: 1108731284-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7879"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Baby picture.... <BR>Chapter 1:  A serial killer is born<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7879-->
<!--Post: 8017--><!--Time: 1108800923-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8017"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 12:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Could BTK be Transgendered? <BR> <BR>Broadly defined, a transgendered person is one whose core gender identity does not coincide with the birth gender.  Transgendered people include transsexuals, cross-dressers, and those whose gender roles are ambiguous. <BR> <BR>Could the X Factor have to do with the research of the X chromosome and the battle over ramifications of a gay gene? <BR> <BR>The Rorschach Comprehensive Psychology Functioning System &#40;Sex Reassignment&#41; mentions the following X Factors: <BR> <BR>X&#43;% = conventional &#40;adequate&#41; <BR>X-% = distorted perception <BR>Xu% = unusual response &#40;adequate but not conventional&#41; <BR> <BR>Gender and Race: &#40;What&#41; Are They? &#40;What&#41; Do We Want Them To Be? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.mit.edu/~shaslang/papers/wigr.html" target=_top>http://www.mit.edu/~shaslang/papers/wigr.html</a> <BR> <BR>Does anyone see any comparisons to BTK? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
